==================================================
2. NEURAL LANGUAGE INTERPRETER
==================================================

A compact sub-1B parameter language model maps
natural-language requests into a structured
intermediate representation.

RESPONSIBILITIES:

- Intent identification
- Entity and relationship extraction
- Goal identification
- Constraint extraction
- Ambiguity detection
- Structured DSL/IR generation
- Result explanation

EXAMPLE IR:

GOAL build_application
REQUIRES authentication
REQUIRES database
CONSTRAINT language = cpp
CONSTRAINT offline_capable = true
SUCCESS_CONDITION tests_pass = true

The language model does not serve as the
authoritative source of logical truth.

Reasoning and verification remain separate
from neural text generation.


==================================================
3. GOAL DECOMPOSITION ENGINE
==================================================

INPUT:
Structured IR

OUTPUT:
Goal dependency graph

FUNCTIONS:

- Decompose complex tasks
- Identify prerequisite goals
- Establish dependency ordering
- Identify parallelisable subgoals
- Track assumptions
- Define measurable success conditions
- Detect missing requirements

GOAL STRUCTURE:

Goal A
  |
  +-- Goal B
  |     |
  |     +-- Goal D
  |
  +-- Goal C
        |
        +-- Goal E

AND/OR relationships distinguish jointly
required prerequisites from alternatives.


