4. SYMBOLIC REASONING ENGINE
==================================================

CORE METHODS:

- Backward chaining
- Forward inference
- First-principles deduction from explicit premises
- Constraint propagation
- Rule application
- Hypothesis generation
- Proof search
- Backtracking
- Search pruning
- Memoisation
- Derivation reuse
- Dependency-aware invalidation

REASONING PIPELINE:

GOAL
  |
  v
BACKWARD CHAINING
  |
  v
PREMISE RETRIEVAL
  |
  v
CONSTRAINT RESOLUTION
  |
  v
FORWARD INFERENCE
  |
  v
DERIVATION CONSTRUCTION
  |
  v
VERIFICATION
  |
  +---- VALID ----> REUSABLE RESULT
  |
  +---- INVALID --> REPAIR / ALTERNATIVE PATH
  |
  +---- UNKNOWN --> UNRESOLVED KNOWLEDGE

Reasoning is resource-bounded.

Failure to find a proof does not establish
that a proposition is impossible.


==================================================
5. CHAIN OF KNOWLEDGE (CoK)
==================================================

The CoK is a persistent directed graph /
hypergraph of structured knowledge.

OBJECT TYPES:

- CLAIM
- FACT
- RULE
- ASSUMPTION
- HYPOTHESIS
- DERIVATION
- EVIDENCE
- GOAL
- ACTION
- EXPERIMENT
- TEST_RESULT
- CONTRADICTION

RELATIONSHIP TYPES:

- REQUIRES
- IMPLIES
- SUPPORTS
- CONTRADICTS
- DEPENDS_ON
- PRODUCES
- TESTS
- ALTERNATIVE_TO

DERIVATION STRUCTURE:

TYPE: DERIVATION
ID: content_hash
CONCLUSION: claim_id
PREMISES: [claim_id, claim_id]
RULE: rule_id
ASSUMPTIONS: [...]
EVIDENCE: [...]
SOURCE_REFERENCES: [...]
VERIFICATION: status
SCHEMA_VERSION: version

KNOWLEDGE STATES:

PROVISIONAL
VERIFIED
DISPUTED
INVALIDATED
UNRESOLVED
ARCHIVED

Each reusable derivation preserves:
- Premises
- Inference rule
- Assumptions
- Supporting evidence
- Source provenance
- Verification status
- Dependency references

Formal validity and empirical truth are
tracked independently.

Contradictions and invalidated derivations
remain traceable.


