==================================================

TARGET SYSTEM:

CPU:
- General-purpose x86-64 / ARM64
- CPU-only execution supported
- Optional GPU acceleration

RAM:
- Target host: 8 GB
- GammaThink target budget: <= 3 GB
- Configurable memory limits

STORAGE:
- SSD-first
- Disk-backed knowledge archives
- IPFS remote extension
- Bounded local caching

RAM COMPONENTS:

- Neural interpreter
- Active reasoning graph
- Search frontier
- Object cache
- Runtime overhead
- Database buffers

SSD COMPONENTS:

- Kiwix ZIM archives
- Local GKS snapshots
- IPFS block cache
- Pinned IPFS content
- Local journal
- Persistent indexes
- Historical derivations

MEMORY POLICY:

- Fixed configurable budget
- Avoid complete archive loading
- Bounded reasoning frontiers
- Bounded cache sizes
- Eviction of inactive objects
- Streaming retrieval
- Batch disk reads
- Compact identifiers

Memory-mapped files still consume
physical RAM when their pages are resident.

The 3 GB target must be validated with
actual interpreter and reasoning workloads.


