==================================================
27. ARCHITECTURAL INVARIANTS
==================================================

- Neural interpretation and symbolic reasoning
  remain independent.

- CPU-only operation remains supported.

- Knowledge archives remain modular,
  indexed and hot-swappable.

- IPFS is an optional storage backend.

- Remote archives appear as logical mounts.

- IPFS snapshots are immutable.

- Local journals provide writable overlays.

- Knowledge size does not require
  proportional RAM growth.

- Remote retrieval is lazy where possible.

- SSD caching remains configurable.

- Object IDs remain independent of IPFS CIDs.

- Snapshot updates are atomic at the
  application catalogue level.

- Trusted updates require publisher
  verification.

- IPFS content integrity is separate
  from knowledge correctness.

- Every derivation preserves assumptions,
  evidence and dependencies.

- Contradictions are not silently overwritten.

- Missing evidence is not equivalent to
  evidence of falsity.

- Failed search is not proof of impossibility.

- Offline operation remains possible with
  locally available dependencies.

- Public contributions require approval.

- Private data is never automatically
  published to IPFS.

- The reasoning graph can grow independently
  of the neural model's weights.


